BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Media School
DTSTART:20260930T193000Z
DTEND:20260930T223000Z
SUMMARY:Exploring Meaning and Recognition Across Immersive Planes
DESCRIPTION:Bring a meaningful keepsake to be digitized and share its sto
 ry for the archive at this 3D scanning drop-in session exploring how pers
 onal objects\, stories\, and emerging tehnologies can shape new forms of 
 participatory archiving. Participants may also experience how these colle
 ctive contributions are being transfored into an interactive installation
  in the KIX Lab.  Megan Young\, senior lecturer of digital art in the Esk
 enazi School\, and Nicole Miller\, director of 3D fabrication and design 
 inquiry labs at the Luddy School\, lead the session.  The event is presen
 ted by the IU Kinetic Immersion and Extended Reality Lab (KIX Lab)\, IU L
 uddy School of Informatics\, Computing and Engineering\, IU Research\, an
 d the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design.  More information i
 s available through Megan Young at young19@iu.edu.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Bring a meaningful keepsake to be digit
 ized and share its story for the archive at this 3D scanning drop-in sess
 ion exploring how personal objects\, stories\, and emerging tehnologies c
 an shape new forms of participatory archiving. Participants may also expe
 rience how these collective contributions are being transfored into an in
 teractive installation in the KIX Lab.</p><p>  Megan Young\, senior lectu
 rer of digital art in the Eskenazi School\, and Nicole Miller\, director 
 of 3D fabrication and design inquiry labs at the Luddy School\, lead the 
 session.</p><p>  The event is presented by the IU Kinetic Immersion and E
 xtended Reality Lab (<span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">KIX Lab)\, 
 IU Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing and Engineering\, IU Research\
 , and the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design.</span></p><p>  
 More information is available through Megan Young at young19@iu.edu.</p>
