SUMMARY:Is AI Going to Kill Journalism?
DESCRIPTION:Robert P. Baird has a Ph.D. in theology from the University o
 f Chicago and has worked as an editor at The New Yorker\, Harper's Magazi
 ne\, The Paris Review\, Chicago Review\, and Esquire. He has published jo
 urnalism\, essays\, and reviews in those magazines and other outlets. He 
 lives in Brooklyn with his wife and children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Robert P. Baird has a Ph.D. in theology
  from the University of Chicago and has worked as an editor at The New Yo
 rker\, Harper's Magazine\, The Paris Review\, Chicago Review\, and Esquir
 e. He has published journalism\, essays\, and reviews in those magazines 
 and other outlets. He lives in Brooklyn with his wife and children.</p>
UID:20261001T150000Z-2430746@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260925T083729Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/mediaiub/event/2430746-is-ai-going-to-kill-jour
 nalism
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T123729Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/45/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,768,768/32704_robert-p-baird-headshot-768x768.rev.179033
 9778.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2430746
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/45/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,768\,768/32704_robert-p-baird-headshot-768x
 768.rev.1790339778.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>A moderated conversation and Q&amp\;A with writer 
 and editor Robert P. Baird examining the opportunities and challenges art
 ificial intelligence presents for journalism\, and exploring its impact o
 n reporting\, intellectual property\, human judgment\, and the future of 
 a reliable information ecosystem.</p>
END:VEVENT
